{
  "protocolVersion": 1,
  "about": [
    "Whole conversations between the editor and the board (SPEC.md §7). Each exchange is a list of steps in order.",
    "{\"editor\": M} is a message the editor sends; {\"board\": M} is one the board must send next.",
    "\"garbled\": true on an editor step: the line reaches the board damaged (the board runner sends a line that isn't base64).",
    "\"lost\": true on a board step: the board sends it but the editor never receives it (the editor runner doesn't deliver it).",
    "\"illegal\": true on an editor step: the board must announce an illegal transition (SPEC §7.6) for it; every other step must announce none. On a board step: the editor must.",
    "{\"editorRaw\": hex}: a frame the board runner sends as-is (board-only exchanges).",
    "{\"editorRaw\": hex} with a frame cut short stands for a line that lost bytes but is still valid base64.",
    "Board messages are compared on every key except free-memory figures and the human-readable error/message text.",
    "\"editor\" at the exchange level says what the editor is asked to do (a deploy or a library), and \"outcome\" what",
    "it must conclude; exchanges without it are board-only. Byte strings are {\"$bytes\": hex}. {\"$flow\": true} stands",
    "for the exchange's compiled \"flowSource\" (the board runner compiles it; the editor runner uses the source's bytes),",
    "and {\"$flowLength\": true} for its length. A board runner starts a fresh listener for each exchange."
  ],
